{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis","id":1091177,"title":"Shuankhsen and Apotheosis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-11T09:47:39-07:00","id":1091177,"title":"Shuankhsen and Apotheosis","content":"Not that it wouldn't be horrifically difficult, given their particular state and...<i>patron</i> ...but still, theoretically, could one of the Shuankhsen break free from Ammut?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:11:25-07:00","id":1091243,"title":"","content":"Isn't it canon that they cannot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:36:10-07:00","id":1091253,"title":"","content":"It is. On top of that, if you were to make it possible, it'd be hugely problematic. Apotheosis requires rebuilding your soul, so getting more pillars. Now look at how Shuankhsen restore their pillars.<br /> <br /> ...yeah. &quot;Get free of Ammut by doing exactly what she wants and eating an absolute metric ton of Mummies.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:50:09-07:00","id":1091260,"title":"","content":"It's possibly even more twisted. The Arisen and the Deceived need to regain their Memory to have a shot at Apotheosis. If we assume that Shuankhsen need to regain their Humanity, that goal might not be attainable after millennia of Soul-eating. With their perfect recall, they don't even get a fresh start, unlike other Mummies. Also, considering that the Apotheosis means different things for the Arisen and the Deceived, Shuankhsen might get something else entirely. Like escape into oblivion. It's arguably an improvement, but still...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T14:39:39-07:00","id":1091274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091253#post1091253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is. On top of that, if you were to make it possible, it'd be hugely problematic. Apotheosis requires rebuilding your soul, so getting more pillars. Now look at how Shuankhsen restore their pillars.<br /> <br /> ...yeah. &quot;Get free of Ammut by doing exactly what she wants and eating an absolute metric ton of Mummies.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like the idea of one reaching Apotheosis by &quot;paying off their debt&quot;, there's a terrifying villian plot right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T15:38:31-07:00","id":1091303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091274#post1091274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I really like the idea of one reaching Apotheosis by &quot;paying off their debt&quot;, there's a terrifying villian plot right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblivion, maybe. Not Apotheosis. That runs counter to its every underlying theme and principle.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Shuankhsen that has deluded itself into thinking it can achieve Apotheosis through doing so. But honestly, why would Ammut cast aside a tool so powerful that it has consumed enough Arisen to get 5 in every Pillar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T16:06:46-07:00","id":1091321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091303#post1091303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oblivion, maybe. Not Apotheosis. That runs counter to its every underlying theme and principle.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Shuankhsen that has deluded itself into thinking it can achieve Apotheosis through doing so. But honestly, why would Ammut cast aside a tool so powerful that it has consumed enough Arisen to get 5 in every Pillar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, whether it will <i>work</i> is kind of incidental to the fact you have a powerful super-undead running around with a plot to devour countless souls.<br /> <br /> And besides, even if it fails it can't make things any <i>worse </i>for the lifeless so hey- worth a shot, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T16:32:26-07:00","id":1091326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091321#post1091321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, whether it will <i>work</i> is kind of incidental to the fact you have a powerful super-undead running around with a plot to devour countless souls.<br /> <br /> And besides, even if it fails it can't make things any <i>worse </i>for the lifeless so hey- worth a shot, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Powerful super-undead trying to devour countless souls&quot; is the default behaviour of any Shuankhsen though. That's not really something special. An Arisen's Pillars are described in the core book as the ultimate prize of any Shuankhsen.<br /> <br /> I don't mind a complimentary reason to try and make life miserable for the Arisen (the good ol' &quot;I was your slave in life and now I want revenge&quot; is a great standby) but let's not act like &quot;Shuankhsen's coming to eat you&quot; is a spectacularly novel bit of villain design <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Personally, I love giving Shuankhsen reasons <i>not</i> to eat a given Mummy. Way more creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T18:55:31-07:00","id":1091378,"title":"","content":"Vile as they can be, Shuankhsen as a whole do have legitimate grievances with the Arisen, and so theoretically could get their due with a minimum of moral erosion.And let's not forget, difficult as it may be, Morality can be raised later. And Ammut may not want to 'cast aside' such an agent, but that's the point of Apotheosis, isn't it? It's not about what Ammut wants, but what the Shuankhsen wants.<br /> <br /> Edit: I've just gone over the Shuankhsen section again, and it doesn't explicitly state anywhere that they can't raise Pillars with Experience. So, there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 05-11-2017, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T19:10:57-07:00","id":1091380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091378#post1091378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vile as they can be, Shuankhsen as a whole do have legitimate grievances with the Arisen, and so theoretically could get their due with a minimum of moral erosion.And let's not forget, difficult as it may be, Morality can be raised later. And Ammut may not want to 'cast aside' such an agent, but that's the point of Apotheosis, isn't it? It's not about what Ammut wants, but what the Shuankhsen wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring explicitly to the idea that a Shuankhsen could achieve Apotheosis by &quot;paying off their debt&quot;, i.e. consuming enough Arisen that their duty to Ammut is fulfilled. That suggested to me that Ammut was being bought off, in spite of the fact that she has no reason to actually accept a Shuankhsen's desire to be free.<br /> <br /> Now, I certainly agree that Shuankhsen are some of the easier enemies in the Chronicles of Darkness to empathise with on an ideological level, but I can't agree that the effort required to reach 25 Pillar dots (21 more than a Shuankhsen begins with) would result in &quot;minimal&quot; moral erosion. We're talking cannibals from a culture that don't see a separation between the physical and the spiritual when it comes to the soul. We're talking the very literal systematic destruction of the souls of others in order to build one's own power. Shuankhsen recover spent Pillar points with actions of violent physical or spiritual betrayal.<br /> <br /> Because of the way Morality works it is theoretically possible that a Shuankhsen could achieve 25 pillar dots without descending to Morality 0, if they pace themselves and spend experience to rebuild their Morality after each loss (assuming that Shuankhsen can spend experience on Morality, it's been a while and I can't actually recall if there's any text preventing that). But I vehemently disagree with the idea that Apotheosis is an appropriate reward for performing, at bare minimum, 21 acts of soul-shredding cannibalism. Whether the Shuankhsen is a good person at the end of it is rather irrelevant, you're predicating your Apotheosis on the performance of extremely harmful acts. That, simply, doesn't fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T19:46:37-07:00","id":1091392,"title":"","content":"My campaign involved a Shuankhsen, once a beloved Arisen meret-mate of the PC, hunting down an exceptionally unique relic they used to protect in hopes it would result in his freedom. It didn't really work.<br /> <br /> I always liked the idea of a Shuankhsen having a way out, even if they partially exist as the opposite 'end-game' of an Arisen's Apotheosis. Still, Mummy is a game about freedom; while I think it might dilute its themes to say even they can become free, I think it might be more in theme to say that they go from one bad option to another.<br /> <br /> Right now they serve the Devourer and life is awful. Then they become free of Ammut just to exist in some other torturous state that they always believed would be better might not be unreasonable. Whether they can reach that unexpected Oblivion or not is one thing, but as long as it doesn't actually redeem them I think is okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T21:25:23-07:00","id":1091416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091380#post1091380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring explicitly to the idea that a Shuankhsen could achieve Apotheosis by &quot;paying off their debt&quot;, i.e. consuming enough Arisen that their duty to Ammut is fulfilled. That suggested to me that Ammut was being bought off, in spite of the fact that she has no reason to actually accept a Shuankhsen's desire to be free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, OK. I see what you meant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, I certainly agree that Shuankhsen are some of the easier enemies in the Chronicles of Darkness to empathise with on an ideological level, but I can't agree that the effort required to reach 25 Pillar dots (21 more than a Shuankhsen begins with) would result in &quot;minimal&quot; moral erosion. We're talking cannibals from a culture that don't see a separation between the physical and the spiritual when it comes to the soul. We're talking the very literal systematic destruction of the souls of others in order to build one's own power. </div> </div> </div>As per the edit to my last post, there's nothing in the rules explicitly forbidding Shuankhsen from raising Pillars with Experience. Using Jaws of the Devourer to steal Pillar dots from Arisen is an alternative that requires no spiritual effort (XP), and is a bonus reward to an action that most Shuankhsen would gleefully perform, given the chance (getting a bit of revenge on an Arisen). It's basically a choice between Hard and Easy and afte all they've been through, it's no wonder that most of them lean towards Easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shuankhsen recover spent Pillar points with actions of violent physical or spiritual betrayal. </div> </div> </div>They can also use their Vices; not the most spiritually healthy option, but potentially more-so than the alternatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because of the way Morality works it is theoretically possible that a Shuankhsen could achieve 25 pillar dots without descending to Morality 0, if they pace themselves and spend experience to rebuild their Morality after each loss (assuming that Shuankhsen can spend experience on Morality, it's been a while and I can't actually recall if there's any text preventing that). But I vehemently disagree with the idea that Apotheosis is an appropriate reward for performing, at bare minimum, 21 acts of soul-shredding cannibalism. Whether the Shuankhsen is a good person at the end of it is rather irrelevant, you're predicating your Apotheosis on the performance of extremely harmful acts. That, simply, doesn't fit. </div> </div> </div>In this context, I think Apotheosis is less a reward and more a loophole to be exploited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T22:30:54-07:00","id":1091428,"title":"","content":"Although I don't see anything either that prevents them <i>explicitly</i> from spending xp to raise Pillars, the text does mention that they need to hunt down and eat somebody in order to fuel their Utterances, and does make a big deal out of that they get Pillars via eating Arisen.<br /> Allowing them to spend Experience for Pillars sounds awfully a lot like it isn't Rules As Intended, and a an oversight/error by the authors; I dunno, maybe they didn't explicitly say it because they didn't think they needed to. I don't think we'll get one in here to say &quot;no&quot; but that's not something they seem <i>supposed</i> to be able to do, from a reading of the section.<br /> Also doing so removes part of the threat; they have to hunt the PCs for power and revenge in equal measure.<br /> <br /> I am not sure what you mean by &quot;more of a loophole;&quot; do you mean a loophole only for the Shuankhsen?<br /> <br /> Tangentially, my reading of Apotheosis is that it's for the Deathless and <i>only</i> the Deathless. The Shuankhsen are Lifeless. It's metaphysically different; they cannot return to life the way the Arisen can. I really like that reading, that Shuankhsen are the opposite opposite of Apotheosis. Makes a lot of sense to me.<br /> <br /> I also wanted to add that the Shan'Iatu tried to pay off Ammut and <i>that did not go so well</i>. I'd be inclined to have a Lifeless who believes vehemently they're paying off the debt, when in fact it's not Indentured Servitude but outright ownership; the sword cannot pay off the owner, as it were.<br /> <br /> Here is a different question: why would you want an NPC who can do this, and what purpose does it serve in the story, <i>and</i> what does it do for your chronicle that a Deceived can't do just as well/better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":".  Edited for errors. 05-12-2017, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T22:39:28-07:00","id":1091430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091416#post1091416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this context, I think Apotheosis is less a reward and more a loophole to be exploited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ben Quo addressed my issues with your prior points (I'll note that in my campaigns I've run Shuankhsen, including my one player Shuankhsen, as only being able to gain Pillars through cannibalism too for precisely the reasons he outlined). I would only add that I suspect the reason it isn't mentioned is because Shuankhsen are intended to be NPCs only and thus there isn't much point in tracking experience. But this... you don't achieve Nirvana through a loophole. Apotheosis isn't a contract you enter into or anything you enter into with an external force. The Heretic, when asked on the subject, explicitly tells player characters that it is a personal path to enlightenment, discarding any idea that there is a set formula that can be repeated to achieve the state.<br /> <br /> Oh, and you can't play rules lawyer in one section (&quot;It doesn't specifically tell me that Shuankhsen can't buy Pillars with experience&quot;) while simultaneously taking a loose interpretation of the rules in another (ignoring that Apotheosis requires a Memory stat and a Judge, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T02:51:24-07:00","id":1091470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091428#post1091428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a different question: why would you want an NPC who can do this, and what purpose does it serve in the story, <i>and</i> what does it do for your chronicle that a Deceived can't do just as well/better?</div> </div> </div> </div>It presents the Shuankhsen as sympathetic villains. We, the players having read the book, know why they're sympathetic, but the Silence prevents them from explaining that to your PCs in-game. Having them yearn for freedom from their cruel taskmaster, mysterious and unknowable as She is to the PCs because of the Silence, is something that many Deathless understand.<br /> <br /> &quot;You know those monstrous crocodile-jawed mummies who are unquestionably evil? Turns out not all of them <i>like</i> being that and want a way out just like us.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T05:02:15-07:00","id":1091483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091470#post1091470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It presents the Shuankhsen as sympathetic villains. We, the players having read the book, know why they're sympathetic, but the Silence prevents them from explaining that to your PCs in-game. Having them yearn for freedom from their cruel taskmaster, mysterious and unknowable as She is to the PCs because of the Silence, is something that many Deathless understand.<br /> <br /> &quot;You know those monstrous crocodile-jawed mummies who are unquestionably evil? Turns out not all of them <i>like</i> being that and want a way out just like us.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Silence stops the Shuankhsen from telling you that they're eating you for a totally sympathetic reason too.<br /> <br /> Besides, revealing that you knew the Shuankhsen as a slave who was slaughtered in life seems like an obvious Memory-related event in any Chronicle, but it's harder to show rather than tell the player about a Shuankhsen Apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T05:30:56-07:00","id":1091491,"title":"","content":"Since Apotheosis (or just high Memory, really) Mummies can recall all the way back to Irem, they might realize what exactly the Shuankhsen are and why they (the Shuankhsen) are hunting them (the Arisen).<br /> <br /> Hmm. Might be an interesting echo/parallel/irony - it takes a Mummy (Apotheosis or no?) to break a Shuankhsen out of their servitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-12-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T05:57:09-07:00","id":1091499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091430#post1091430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't achieve Nirvana through a loophole. Apotheosis isn't a contract you enter into or anything you enter into with an external force. The Heretic, when asked on the subject, explicitly tells player characters that it is a personal path to enlightenment, discarding any idea that there is a set formula that can be repeated to achieve the state.<br /> <br /> Oh, and you can't play rules lawyer in one section (&quot;It doesn't specifically tell me that Shuankhsen can't buy Pillars with experience&quot;) while simultaneously taking a loose interpretation of the rules in another (ignoring that Apotheosis requires a Memory stat and a Judge, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, in this context I say 'Apotheosis' as shorthand for breaking free of Ammut's influence, just as the Arisen do with the Judges and the Deceived with the tem-akhs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T06:07:48-07:00","id":1091502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091499#post1091499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear, in this context I say 'Apotheosis' as shorthand for breaking free of Ammut's influence, just as the Arisen do with the Judges and the Deceived with the tem-akhs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Apotheosis is what the game calls that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:59:27-07:00","id":1091594,"title":"","content":"Though I appreciate your point, Reseru, it doesn't answer why the Deceived work just as well, if not better. They are on equal footing with the Guilds; they're the deep end, as their book expresses. They even have a mirrored Apotheosis state, and they can't become Lifeless - arguably, they are living their own fail state (with an Affinity to give into it!).<br /> <br /> You can have then your freedom too, but as mentioned - they don't get to forget.<br /> If someone had eaten ten thousand child hearts and asked me to raise their morality, I'd say no. How do you rationalize that? How do you make that up on anything less than an eternity, with Ammut still chewing on you?<br /> I run Mummy with a 2e hack; this removes some of the issue (as it's easier to rationalize balancing out Integrity) but that too precludes the moral realizations of Memory.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Judges punish the Arisen for daring to act human; the Shuankhsen get rewarded for tormenting and opposing the Arisen.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm trying to say that they are already tragic. Nothing can add to that tragedy; they're already slaves sold to a terrible power to pay for making their whip-masters demigods. Like, that sucks. That sucks so much, and then after however long that torture was - The Rite of Return broke time, so I'm going to say &quot;lifetimes&quot; - Ammut spat them back out and said &quot;k go break shit. Get revenge if you want.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to enhance their tragedy, I'm not sure Apotheosis is the way to do it.<br /> I make my Shuankhsen antagonists deeply connected to the PCs personal lives. I make them seeking &quot;righteous&quot; vengeance. I don't make them anything but monsters - and they are already apex monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":".  Edited for Errors 05-12-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T11:00:08-07:00","id":1091620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091502#post1091502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Apotheosis is what the game calls that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then where did that &quot;Finding Nirvana&quot; comment come from? Shuankhsen Apotheosis isn't Nirvana; at best, it's trading Hell for mere Purgatory.<br /> <br /> And Ben Quo, I see what you're getting at, But would someone who ate the hearts of ten thousand children really be the type of person who'd seek Apotheosis in the first place, never mind whatever the Shuankhsen's watered-down equivalent would be? And even if they did, just because such an act is theoretically <i>possible</i> doesn't mean they'd be able to actually <i>achieve</i> it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T12:16:34-07:00","id":1091654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091620#post1091620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then where did that &quot;Finding Nirvana&quot; comment come from? Shuankhsen Apotheosis isn't Nirvana; at best, it's trading Hell for mere Purgatory.<br /> <br /> And Ben Quo, I see what you're getting at, But would someone who ate the hearts of ten thousand children really be the type of person who'd seek Apotheosis in the first place, never mind whatever the Shuankhsen's watered-down equivalent would be? And even if they did, just because such an act is theoretically <i>possible</i> doesn't mean they'd be able to actually <i>achieve</i> it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I appreciate those counter-points. I think part of the Shuankhsen condition is that it already <i>is</i> the opposite of Apotheosis, so pursuing homebrew of an Apotheosis-equivalent for them would necessitate some very different ideas. Also, the game is pretty clear that Ammut never lets go of what is hers, and she thinks <i>everything</i> is hers to devour. I'm not sure how you'd make a space for it in the game, besides just bottoming out Morality/Integrity and becoming a hungry vessel that is too empty to realize it's a slave (which again can already be expressed with the Deceived).<br /> <br /> Can I ask again, what kind of system and themes are you going for with this? Like, what roll does it fill in your campaign?<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm also not of the opinion that the Shuankhsen aren't ever really &quot;good.&quot; They're tragic, because they were people used as magical <i>trade currency,</i> and that permanently messed them up. Even some of the Shuankhsen examples we have aren't really &quot;people;&quot; they're once-people who have been transformed into Lovecraftian monsters that have a vague person-mask (and perso-suit, since they automatically corpse-hop without even needing a cult to call them back).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 05-12-2017, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T14:04:29-07:00","id":1091695,"title":"","content":"For me, at least, the point of an Apotheosis equivalent for Shuankhsen would be for them to have a hope spot. They were completely shafted by powers beyond their choice or control. Maybe, just maybe, having an out would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T14:34:08-07:00","id":1091709,"title":"","content":"Just so! They may wind up weaker in Sekhem, and on just about <i>everyone's</i> shit-list, but they will have reclaimed their self-determination, and that is no small thing.<br /> <br /> As for Ammut &quot;never letting go&quot;, well, one of the game's core themes is Nothing Lasts Forever. Not even undead slavery to a Black Hole Oblivion Goddess. And if some of the Shuankhsen actually are capable of achieving their freedom, why should Ammut care? They'll come back to her eventually. Everything will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T17:30:46-07:00","id":1091776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091620#post1091620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then where did that &quot;Finding Nirvana&quot; comment come from? Shuankhsen Apotheosis isn't Nirvana; at best, it's trading Hell for mere Purgatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is a personal quest to achieve a state of release from the cycle of rebirth. Seemed like an obvious reference point to me, though I'll happily acknowledge it isn't a 1:1 comparison.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the trajectory, the mechanics of building your Pillars and Memory directly translate into the more philosophical concepts of (respectively) restoring your soul and learning who you are. They represent personal, internal growth and enlightenment. &quot;Loopholes&quot; are not thematically appropriate. Even if all enlightenment gets you is a slightly less miserable existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091709#post1091709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so! They may wind up weaker in Sekhem, and on just about <i>everyone's</i> shit-list, but they will have reclaimed their self-determination, and that is no small thing.<br /> <br /> As for Ammut &quot;never letting go&quot;, well, one of the game's core themes is Nothing Lasts Forever. Not even undead slavery to a Black Hole Oblivion Goddess. And if some of the Shuankhsen actually are capable of achieving their freedom, why should Ammut care? They'll come back to her eventually. Everything will.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Nothing lasts forever, not even being consumed by the embodiment of entropy who is the reason nothing lasts forever.&quot; Really?<br /> <br /> You're not really addressing Ben Quo's point though of what this gives you in the context of the narrative, particularly when you have the Deceived on hand. It gives Shuankhsen a sense of hope? We're talking NPCs that aren't exactly allowed to be open about their motives or emotions. If you do manage to find an elegant way of revealing that the Shuankhsen may have an &quot;out&quot;, what does that give you in return for lessening the tragedy of the Shuankhsen's condition? You've just added an addendum to what is arguably the game's only true failure state, and it's an addendum that is almost nonsensical thematically (causing harm to achieve Apotheosis), so I'm hoping it's giving you something pretty substantial that your players have been crying out for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T18:18:32-07:00","id":1091783,"title":"","content":"Something interesting to consider is if a Shuankhsen did achieve their own version of Apotheosis, they would have done it by essentially cobbling a complete soul out of that of countless others. That could lead to something weird, like being tormented by echos and memories of the people they devoured. They escaped Ammut, but they couldn't escape their sins.<br /> <br /> That's just an idea that came to me. I think &quot;it's impossible&quot; is kind of a boring answer (even if it is probably true), Trying to figure out what would be the end result is much more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T22:50:08-07:00","id":1091831,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that &quot;It's impossible&quot; isn't a boring answer because, again, the Arisen can become Shuankhsen. They can join their fellow slaves in an eternal hell. To address the purgatory analogy: the game already has that; it's being one of the Deathless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 05-14-2017, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T19:01:08-07:00","id":1092181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1091776#post1091776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not really addressing Ben Quo's point though of what this gives you in the context of the narrative, particularly when you have the Deceived on hand. It gives Shuankhsen a sense of hope? We're talking NPCs that aren't exactly allowed to be open about their motives or emotions. If you do manage to find an elegant way of revealing that the Shuankhsen may have an &quot;out&quot;, what does that give you in return for lessening the tragedy of the Shuankhsen's condition? You've just added an addendum to what is arguably the game's only true failure state, and it's an addendum that is almost nonsensical thematically (causing harm to achieve Apotheosis), so I'm hoping it's giving you something pretty substantial that your players have been crying out for.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I'd say the Arisen condition is a Failure State across the board, but then, I'm a firm believer in personal autonomy, so I'm biased.<br /> Second, I fall back to my earlier statement that using Jaws of the Devourer is the quick and easy way, as opposed to the measured re-discovery of the self; or, in the Shuankhsen's case, <i>reclamation </i>of the self. That said, I don't think stealing Pillars from Arisen is as much an ethical stumbling block as, say, creating Fasad or killing mortals to regain Pillar points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T20:55:07-07:00","id":1092213,"title":"","content":"I feel like everyone is just dancing around semantics here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T21:13:21-07:00","id":1092215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1092181#post1092181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, I'd say the Arisen condition is a Failure State across the board, but then, I'm a firm believer in personal autonomy, so I'm biased.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your opinion on the merits of being Arisen isn't really the point though, and is outright wrong from a game design perspective. Being an Arisen cannot be a failure state because that's the default mode of play. More than that, there are ways to move on from being Arisen, one of which, Apotheosis, is arguably the game's &quot;win condition&quot;. There is only one way an Arisen character can become unplayable, and that is to fall and become Shuankhsen, making it the failure state.<br /> <br /> When it happened in my campaign I allowed the Shuankhsen character to remain playable because there were some ideas I still wanted to explore (and also because the game was rapidly nearing its end) but I didn't try to shy away from portraying that moment as a fall, a tragic end to an Arisen. That word &quot;end&quot; was important, there is a finality to that moment.<br /> <br /> My original question was asking you what you feel you gain thematically by diluting the game's themes in this respect and providing a way of mitigating the &quot;you lose&quot; ending baked into Mummy. It's similar to giving, say, Changelings a way to recover from being recaptured by the True Fae. I'm not sure it makes the game stronger...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1092181#post1092181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I fall back to my earlier statement that using Jaws of the Devourer is the quick and easy way, as opposed to the measured re-discovery of the self; or, in the Shuankhsen's case, <i>reclamation </i>of the self. That said, I don't think stealing Pillars from Arisen is as much an ethical stumbling block as, say, creating Fasad or killing mortals to regain Pillar points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I'd put the violation and cannibalisation of another being's soul on much the same level as murder or spiritual enslavement. On the Morality chart I'd certainly have it no higher than a Morality 3 sin.<br /> <br /> Sadly, we can only agree to disagree when it comes to using experience to restore pillars. In the (sadly, far too few) conversations I've had with writers who have worked on Mummy I did actually talk about the presentation of Shuankhsen, and from what has been said I would feel very confident in saying that cannibalisation is the only method of gaining Pillars for Shuankhsen. And I would maintain that the reason it's not mentioned one way or the other in the core book comes down simply to what I was saying above. Shuankhsen are the failure state. You aren't meant to play them. Why would they need to address the expenditure of experience for characters that aren't going to be earning experience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T11:54:58-07:00","id":1092894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1092215#post1092215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, we can only agree to disagree when it comes to using experience to restore pillars. In the (sadly, far too few) conversations I've had with writers who have worked on Mummy I did actually talk about the presentation of Shuankhsen, and from what has been said I would feel very confident in saying that cannibalisation is the only method of gaining Pillars for Shuankhsen. And I would maintain that the reason it's not mentioned one way or the other in the core book comes down simply to what I was saying above. Shuankhsen are the failure state. You aren't meant to play them. Why would they need to address the expenditure of experience for characters that aren't going to be earning experience?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you're right; providing Shuankhsen with an Apotheosis-style 'out' to their condition, while allowing for some intriguing plot hooks, doesn't really add anything to the narrative of the game. Maybe I'm just being overly sentimental about the whole thing, but I just hate that they're doomed to be cannibalistic monstrosities for all eternity due to pure circumstance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T13:17:38-07:00","id":1092925,"title":"","content":"The real question is if we do really want a Shuankhsen which has managed to free himself from Ammut. I mean, sure, the Arisen and the Deceived are all uplifted by achieving their freedom, but Apotheosis-like event doesn't mean the being in question has to become &quot;nicer&quot;. As far as we all know, the potential Shuankhsen which may free himself from the Devourer would become a ravaging force of destruction, uncontrolled by any force on heaven or earth. The cannibal hymn? That's not Unas. That's what his teacher may <i>be</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T16:31:28-07:00","id":1093008,"title":"","content":"I don't think it counts as Apotheosis, but one of my game's mummies is being driven a bit crazy because his two wives are trying to convince him to end the rite of return. The Deceived AND shuanksen both think that destroying the Judges will free them of the rite. For the Shuanksen, she believes that if the Judges are gone, she could escape Ammut and become Deathless. She thinks the Arisen escape her every time they Arise, and believes the Judges are what keeps her from doing the same.<br /> <br /> While she is almost certainly wrong, its possible that her idea isn't unsound. It would be less of a personal quest of enlightenment, and more of a cosmic level endgame event, but... its possible something as big and momentous as the rite of return could be done again. A dangerous sorcerer or elder god might be able to take remnants from ammut's jaw and referee them. Provided there is something left of that person--and Ammut made that possible by not entirely devouring them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T17:12:47-07:00","id":1093026,"title":"","content":"In regards to the game's themes, Apotheosis is about achieving freedom from their masters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:32:03-07:00","id":1094145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1091177-shuankhsen-and-apotheosis?p=1093026#post1093026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the game's themes, Apotheosis is about achieving freedom from their masters</div> </div> </div> </div>A Shuankhsen who has achieved Apotheosis might be mostly unchanged, with the main benefit being Ammut can no longer punish them and they can permanently die. Because Ammut can't punish them, they could become a source of information on Irem, the Shuankhsen state, and Ammut while also coming off as incredibly untrustworthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T15:09:03-07:00","id":1094315,"title":"","content":"I'd almost rather reverse things: instead of remembering everything they <i>lose</i> memory of their time as a Shuankhsen. In this case, freedom from the Silence becomes moot - things don't become easy, with ex-Shuankhsen just going around to Arisen telling them stuff about Irem (actually they'd probably still be very spiteful).<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of a Shuankhsen's Apotheosis just being able to die. Instead of some high enlightened state of freedom they only receive one brief moment, where they must decide to either go back to Ammut and keep on living or kill themselves and be free of it all forever. It's a tragic choice, and the Shuankhsen who stick around must be really vile (or desperate for life, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T08:57:44-07:00","id":1097146,"title":"","content":"Can Shuankhsen eat each other for Pillars? I can't recall off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T09:40:20-07:00","id":1097165,"title":"","content":"I was wondering myself. &quot;Sothis Ascends&quot; has this tidbit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothis Ascends p.22</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">His first target awoke and nearly destroyed him, prompting him to ally with eight other Shuankhsen \u2014 there were more, but many early Lifeless prey on each other, and some were too traumatized by their time in Ammut\u2019s grasp to understand his offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, this can refer to preying on Sekhem instead of Pillars and doesn't clarify whether Shuankhsen are even edible as opposed to just tantalising. Also, Ammut is really unlikely to approve.<br /> <br /> If Shuankhsen can indeed eat each other's Pillars, that not only provides them with acceptable (for the sake of argument) targets, but also means a Shuankhsen could be repeatedly eaten into oblivion. Ironically, escaping their cycle would mean repeatedly succumbing to the very thing that started it in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:12:55-07:00","id":1097253,"title":"","content":"Core book, page 194; it specifically says they can &quot;technically eat each other.&quot; Since they have Sekhem, they can eat each other's Sekhem, and likely each other's Pillars. I thought I recall reading something about how a Mummy can't lose their last dot in their Decree, which I'd assume also applies to Remnant, but I can't figure out where that was right now (it may have just been head-canon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 05-27-2017, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}